================================================================
1. DATABASE CONTENTS — Open Database License (ODbL) v1.0
================================================================

The INCIDB database (the `products`, `ingredients`, `brands`,
`product_ingredients` and `ingredient_name_map` tables, in all CSV and Apache
Parquet exports and in the preview samples) is a derivative of the Open Beauty
Facts database and is therefore licensed under the Open Database License
(ODbL) v1.0:

    https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

You are free to share, create works from, and adapt the database — including
for commercial purposes — provided that you:

  (a) ATTRIBUTE Open Beauty Facts contributors and INCIDB;
  (b) SHARE-ALIKE — if you publicly use or distribute an adapted version of
      the database, you offer that adapted database under ODbL; and
  (c) KEEP-OPEN — you do not use technological measures that restrict others
      from obtaining the database in an ODbL-licensed form.

Product data © Open Beauty Facts contributors (https://openbeautyfacts.org),
licensed under ODbL. The regulatory and chemical fields (CosIng functional
categories, CAS and EC numbers, chemical descriptions, restrictions, Annex
II-VI membership, and the EU Annex III fragrance-allergen flags) are factual
data compiled from the European Commission CosIng database and the EU
Cosmetics Regulation, reused with attribution under the Commission's
public-sector information reuse policy. The US FDA has not yet published its
MoCRA fragrance-allergen list, so no field in this database is derived from
one. `comedogenic_rating` is transcribed from published literature (Fulton,
1989) and `is_fungal_acne_trigger` is a cited rule-derived flag; both are
informational only and are not medical, safety or regulatory-compliance
advice.

